WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.897
Welcome back to the threshold of The Signal.

00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:11.500
This page appears after a return from Whop, but a return alone is not proof that your free gate is open.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.293
Sign in to the Whop account you used and look for The Signal in its library.

00:00:17.293 --> 00:00:22.724
The Signal is intended as a free room, with no card requirement or recurring charge.

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:27.431
Once Whop confirms access, begin with Dispatches to see announcements and new realms.

00:00:27.431 --> 00:00:31.414
Then open the First Vision for an introduction to the chambers.

00:00:31.414 --> 00:00:39.741
The named rooms form a map through the story: the Signal, the Realm, the Process, the Records, the Session and the Field Journal.

00:00:39.741 --> 00:00:43.000
Move among them at the pace your account allows.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.330
The calendar marks the rhythm of upcoming work.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.534
The Sanctuary gives travellers a shared place to return between visions.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:58.650
Neither this film nor its address can unlock those rooms for you; the verified Whop account is the source of access.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:03.602
If your library shows The Signal, open it there and take your time with the first vision.

00:01:03.602 --> 00:01:07.388
If you cannot find it, check the account and email used at entry.

00:01:07.388 --> 00:01:12.922
For help, contact Numinous support with your Whop receipt or confirmation, never a password or a full card number.

00:01:12.922 --> 00:01:17.000
The free gate is the beginning, not an obligation to buy the next one.
